# Local overrides. The deployed site does not need this file — netlify.toml sets
# VITE_WAITLIST_FORM, and the API key lives in Netlify's environment, never a
# repo file. Never put a real key here either: anything that was ever in a
# local .env is rotated (docs/SECURITY.md, docs/RECOVERY.md scenario 10).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The domain. Unset, the app calls itself joinniyyah.com (src/lib/site.ts),
# the address we own, baked into every link it hands out and every share
# card. Set it only to move: if the domain were ever lost, set this to the new
# host (or getniyyah.netlify.app, which keeps serving) and redeploy —
# docs/RECOVERY.md, scenario 8. See docs/CONTROL.md.
# VITE_SITE_HOST=joinniyyah.com

# Where a signup reaches a human when the form is not configured. The default,
# salaam@joinniyyah.com, is only real once that domain receives mail — until
# then set this to an address a person reads (docs/DEPLOY.md).
# VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=salaam@joinniyyah.com

# Netlify Forms: the form name signups are posted to. Set in netlify.toml for
# the deploy; set it here only if you're pointing a local build at Netlify.
# VITE_WAITLIST_FORM=niyyah-waitlist

# Or any endpoint that accepts a JSON POST of { contact, code, scene, gender, hardestPart, at }
# — Airtable, a Google Apps Script, a Supabase function, your own /api route.
# Used only when VITE_WAITLIST_FORM is unset.
VITE_WAITLIST_URL=

# With neither set the app will NOT pretend anyone joined: the signup card falls
# back to a mailto so nothing is silently lost.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is deliberately NOT listed here. It belongs only in Netlify's
# environment — plaintext to the team on the free plan, which refuses the
# secret scope (docs/DEPLOY.md), so rotation is the control — because it is read by netlify/functions/guide.ts
# on the server and must never reach the browser bundle or the repository.
#
# Setting it switches the live Guide on, which means members' answers start
# leaving their device — so the Trust screen's privacy copy must be rewritten in
# the same change. See the README.
#
# FOUNDER_KEY is not listed here either. It gates every readout — the ladder,
# the full tally on the door, the couple tally, the pool, the backup, the
# safety queue, the guide's health check — behind `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.
# Unset means CLOSED: every readout answers 401 until it is set
# (netlify/shared/founder.ts). This file said the opposite until
# 2026-09-23, long after that stopped being true (docs/SECURITY.md, O4).
# Use a long random value (32+ characters), set it in Netlify's environment
# and as a GitHub Actions secret of the same name (the health run reads
# /health with it), and confirm a bare GET on /health returns 401. See
# docs/DEPLOY.md and docs/OPS.md.
